## Collision guardrails

- **ai-council** — does not own: Evidence Pack construction; context gateway; implementation. Explicit invocation only.
- **ai-humanize** — does not own: authorship claims; detector defeat; generic proofreading-only.
- **artifact-acceptance** — does not own: software release verdicts; initial editorial review; consequential strategic decisions.
- **benchmark-curator** — does not own: model experiment execution; rubric design; skill editing.
- **brief-architect** — does not own: final artifact production; broad product discovery; consequential strategic decisions.
- **cometweb-context** — does not own: evidence packs; domain decisions; release gates; outbound copy.
- **competitive-intelligence** — does not own: strategic GO/NO_GO; pricing decision.
- **content-reviewer** — does not own: adversarial roasting; full content rewrites; final publication acceptance.
- **content-roaster** — does not own: scientific peer review; repository/code critique; rewrite-only editing.
- **content-writer** — does not own: persuasion-first campaign copy; primary evidence research; publication release orchestration.
- **customer-ops** — does not own: release gate; Council decision.
- **design-partner-finder** — does not own: cold outbound copy; Council pricing.
- **ebook-publisher** — does not own: independent evidence truth certification; public publishing authorization; host installation; generic blog writing.
- **evidence-researcher** — does not own: final GO/NO_GO; release verdict; context-only refresh.
- **feedback-integrator** — does not own: silent self-modification; single-signal generalization; product or research analytics.
- **longform-publisher** — does not own: primary evidence research; generic prose humanization; DOCX/PDF rendering internals.
- **portfolio-operator** — does not own: deep single-product sequencing; release GO/NO_GO; specialist implementation.
- **product-operator** — does not own: from-scratch roadmap; RC GO/NO_GO.
- **product-teardown** — does not own: owned-repo roadmap; release gate.
- **quality-loop-operator** — does not own: general multi-skill orchestration; consequential strategy decisions; software production-readiness verdicts.
- **release-readiness** — does not own: weekly priorities; whole-project baseline.
- **repair-operator** — does not own: initial broad audit; inventing new requirements; production release verdicts.
- **repo-roaster** — does not own: whole-project roadmapping; runtime web QA; final production release verdicts.
- **repo-to-roadmap** — does not own: weekly sprint ops; RC ship gate.
- **rubric-designer** — does not own: judging the candidate; writing the artifact; running empirical skill benchmarks.
- **science-roaster** — does not own: generic content critique; repository/code review; research-program planning.
- **seo-geo-aeo-maxxing** — does not own: Evidence Pack construction; click-through QA.
- **skill-auditor** — does not own: editing the audited skill; empirical behavioral benchmarking; production release verdicts.
- **skill-evaluator** — does not own: static package audits; editing the skill; universal superiority claims.
- **skill-orchestrator** — does not own: domain skill contracts; Council policy; release gates.
- **skill-orchestrator-multiagent** — does not own: separate planning model.
- **web-app-auditor** — does not own: release verdict; SEO scoring.

